  "notes": "IMPERIAL chart converted exactly: capacities lbs x 1000 x 0.45359237 -> t, rounded to 0.1 t; boom lengths and radii ft x 0.3048 -> m, rounded to 0.01 m (e.g. 7.5 ft = 2.29 m, 8.2 ft = 2.5 m, 9.8 ft = 2.99 m). The imperial chart is itself a conversion of Tadano's metric chart, so small rounding differences vs. the metric original are possible. No official metric ATF 100G-4 datasheet could be downloaded (tadano.com upload/docs links now return HTML; Tadano Europe page has no PDF). 36.4* ft over-rear column (excluded, kips@ft): 220.5@7.5, 198.4@8.2, 179.9@9.8, 164.5@11.5, 150.6@13.1, 138.2@14.8, 127.4@16.4, 110.2@19.7, 93.7@23, 80.7@26.2, 54.9@29.5 (220.5 kips = 100 t at 7.5 ft over rear with additional lifting equipment; ** = with additional lifting equipment also at 9.8 ft for 36.4 ft 360° column: 167.8 kips). The 7.5 ft and 8.2 ft rows are empty in all 360° columns and were dropped. Headline 100 t (110 US ton) is over-rear only. Remarks p.22: ratings per ASME B30.5-1.1; weight of hook blocks, slings etc. is part of the load and must be deducted. Same chart values also in Tadano America datasheet https://www.coastlinecd.com/pdf/Tadano%20ATF-100G-4-Imperial_02_2015.pdf p.5 (radii rounded to whole ft there, booms 48.5/60.6/72.6/84.7/120.9/133.0/145.1 ft); the Sterling copy with 0.1 ft radii was used for the chart. Dimensions and specs from the Coastline/Tadano America datasheet: p.2 (mm) overall length 12846 incl. boom overhang (13051 top chain), carrier 10750, boom overhang 2096; axle spacing 2970 (front to axle 1), 1700, 2440, 1750; rear overhang 1890 (+401); slewing centre 145 behind axle 3 (derived 7255 from carrier front); outriggers 8540 longitudinal (5680.5 + 2859.5 / 5389.5 + 3150.5), transverse 7200 (5000/6000 intermediate); height 3925 (445/95R25); width 2750 (445/95R25) / 3000 (525/80R25); superstructure rear radii R3913 / R3700 / R3242 (largest taken as tail radius). p.25: 6-section boom (1 base + 5 telescoping), tyres 445/95 R 25 width 2.75 m. Counterweight 22.5 t = 1.0 + 2.5 + 1.6 + 1.6 + 0.9 + 3 x 2.9 + 6.2 t (p.23). Base machine without counterweight/fuel/driver 84,502 lbs (38.3 t); operating weight in full configuration not stated."
